<title>LEBANON: Lebanese financial markets open despite strike.</title>
<headline>Lebanese financial markets open despite strike.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most Lebanese banks and financial markets opened on Thursday despite a general strike call made by opposition groups in protest against the policies of Prime Minister Rafik al-Hariri.</p>
<p>In Beirut, the central bank opened and most of the capital's commercial banks followed suit. Foreign exchange brokers at some leading banks were in their offices when Reuters called and trading activities were normal at the Beirut Stock Exchange (BSE).</p>
</text>
